/// `ps -ax` for `zsh|bash` — which always matches every unrelated shell already running on the
/// machine (a real CI/dev box has dozens). That makes a manual run's "no shells left behind"
/// judgment call unreliable, and an automated one worthless. This test instead spawns the pane's
/// shell with `exec -a <uniqueMarker>`, so `argv[0]` is a token that cannot collide with anything
/// else on the system, and polls for that EXACT token.
///
/// **Why quit via `XCUIApplication.terminate()`, not a force-quit or workroom-switch.** Those two
/// paths stay in the manual `QA-libghostty.md` checklist — this test covers specifically the normal
/// UI-quit teardown path (`WorkroomApp.applicationWillTerminate`'s documented no-mass-free
/// rationale: the process exits, the OS reclaims libghostty's memory and closes the PTYs, every
/// child shell gets SIGHUP exactly as a manual `ghostty_surface_free` would deliver). A bad IO patch
/// is exactly the kind of change that could make that SIGHUP never arrive, or arrive after libghostty
/// itself has already torn down the surface it came from.
///
/// **Proof this can actually go red, not just green** (design requirement — a test that was never
/// capable of failing is worse than no test): `testMarkerDetectionCatchesAGenuineOrphan_designProof`
/// spawns the SAME marked shell but immune to the SIGHUP a normal quit sends (`trap '' HUP` +
/// `disown`), so it survives quitting regardless of whether the app's teardown is healthy. Run once
/// while writing this test, it failed exactly as expected — the assertion mechanism can tell a real
/// orphan from a clean exit. That proof doesn't depend on the engine at all (a disowned, HUP-immune
/// process survives any parent's exit, healthy or not), so it is NOT re-run on every `make app-uitest`
/// — re-running it every time would only prove `trap`/`disown` still work, not that the app's
/// teardown does. It stays here, commented with its one-time result, as the design record.
final class GhosttyOrphanShellUITests: XCTestCase {
  override func setUp() {
    super.setUp()
    continueAfterFailure = false
  }

  private func launchedApp() -> XCUIApplication {
    let app = XCUIApplication()
    app.launchArguments += ["-WorkroomUITestFixture", "1"]
